              "question": null,
              "answer": "The separation between man and woman legitimately united by marriage cannot be done, except on account of adultery, as it is taught by our Lord (Matthew 5:32; Matthew 19:9). And the separation can not only be made by this cause, but also, with the cause properly examined by authorities, the non-guilty party, if he cannot contain himself should marry, as it is taught by Saint Ambrose’s commentary on 1 Corinthians 7. The magistrate however must proceed in this matter with mature counsel.",
