              "id": "a14_1",
              "label": "1",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "Saint Paul, when teaching that the bishop must be husband of one wife (1 Timothy 3:2), is not saying that to marry again is not proper, but he is condemning bigamy, which attracted many in those times; nevertheless, we will leave the concluding judgment on this matter to ones more versed in Holy Scripture, and we do not found our faith on this point.",
