        {
          "number": "2",
          "title": "The First Part : Of The Misery Of Man",
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "q3",
              "label": "Q3",
              "question": "How do you come to know your misery?",
              "answer": "The law of God tells me.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.3_20",
                      "display": "Romans 3:20"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.7_7-25",
                      "display": "Romans 7:7-25"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q4",
              "label": "Q4",
              "question": "What does God’s law require of us?",
              "answer": "Christ teaches us this in summary in Matthew 22:37-40 - “You shall love the Lord your God with all your heart, and with all your soul, and with all your mind, and with all your strength. This is the great and first commandment. And a second is like it, you shall love your neighbour as yourself. On these two commandments depend all the law and the prophets.”",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Leviticus.19_18",
                      "display": "Leviticus 19:18"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Deuteronomy.6_5",
                      "display": "Deuteronomy 6:5"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q5",
              "label": "Q5",
              "question": "Can you live up to all this perfectly?",
              "answer": "No. I have a natural tendency to hate God and my neighbour.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Genesis.6_5",
                      "display": "Genesis 6:5"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Jeremiah.17_9",
                      "display": "Jeremiah 17:9"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.3_9-20~23",
                      "display": "Romans 3:9-20,23"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.7_23~24",
                      "display": "Romans 7:23,24"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 5,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.8_7",
                      "display": "Romans 8:7"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 6,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Ephesians.2_1-3",
                      "display": "Ephesians 2:1-3"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 7,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Titus.3_3",
                      "display": "Titus 3:3"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 8,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.John.1_8~10",
                      "display": "1 John 1:8,10"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q6",
              "label": "Q6",
              "question": "Did God create man so wicked and perverse?",
              "answer": "No. God created man good and in his own image, that is, in true righteousness and holiness, so that he might truly know God his creator, love him with all his heart, and live with him in eternal happiness for His praise and glory.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Genesis.1_26~27~31",
                      "display": "Genesis 1:26,27,31"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Psalm.8",
                      "display": "Psalm 8"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Ephesians.4_24",
                      "display": "Ephesians 4:24"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Colossians.3_10",
                      "display": "Colossians 3:10"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q7",
              "label": "Q7",
              "question": "Then where does man’s corrupt nature come from?",
              "answer": "From the fall and disobedience of our first parents, Adam and Eve, in Paradise. This fall has so poisoned our nature that we are born sinners - corrupt from conception on.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Genesis.3",
                      "display": "Genesis 3"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Psalm.51_5",
                      "display": "Psalm 51:5"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.5_12~18~19",
                      "display": "Romans 5:12,18,19"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q8",
              "label": "Q8",
              "question": "But are we so corrupt that we are totally unable to do any good and inclined toward all evil?",
              "answer": "Yes, unless we are born again, by the Spirit of God.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Genesis.6_5",
                      "display": "Genesis 6:5"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Genesis.8_21",
                      "display": "Genesis 8:21"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Job.14_4",
                      "display": "Job 14:4"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Isaiah.53_6",
                      "display": "Isaiah 53:6"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 5,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "John.3_3-5",
                      "display": "John 3:3-5"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q9",
              "label": "Q9",
              "question": "But doesn’t God do man an injustice by requiring in his law what man is unable to do?",
              "answer": "No, God created man with the ability to keep the law. Man, however, tempted by the devil, in reckless disobedience, robbed himself and his descendants of these gifts.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Genesis.1_31",
                      "display": "Genesis 1:31"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Genesis.3_6~13",
                      "display": "Genesis 3:6,13"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "John.8_44",
                      "display": "John 8:44"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.5_12~18~19",
                      "display": "Romans 5:12,18,19"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 5,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Ephesians.4_24",
                      "display": "Ephesians 4:24"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q10",
              "label": "Q10",
              "question": "Will God permit such disobedience and rebellion to go unpunished?",
              "answer": "Certainly not. He is terribly angry about the sin we are born with as well as the sins we personally commit. As a just judge He punishes them now and in eternity. He has declared: Cursed be every one who does not abide by all things written in the book of the law, and do them.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Exodus.34_7",
                      "display": "Exodus 34:7"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Deuteronomy.27_26",
                      "display": "Deuteronomy 27:26"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Psalm.5_4-6",
                      "display": "Psalm 5:4-6"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Nahum.1_2",
                      "display": "Nahum 1:2"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 5,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.1_18",
                      "display": "Romans 1:18"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 6,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Galatians.3_10",
                      "display": "Galatians 3:10"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 7,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Ephesians.5_6",
                      "display": "Ephesians 5:6"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 8,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Hebrews.9_27",
                      "display": "Hebrews 9:27"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q11",
              "label": "Q11",
              "question": "But isn’t God also merciful?",
              "answer": "God is certainly merciful, but He is also just. His justice demands that sin, committed against His supreme majesty, be punished with the supreme penalty - eternal punishment of body and soul.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Exodus.34_6~7",
                      "display": "Exodus 34:6,7"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Deuteronomy.7_9-11",
                      "display": "Deuteronomy 7:9-11"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Psalm.5_4-6",
                      "display": "Psalm 5:4-6"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Psalm.103_8~9",
                      "display": "Psalm 103:8,9"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 5,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Matthew.25_35-46",
                      "display": "Matthew 25:35-46"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 6,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Hebrews.10_30~31",
                      "display": "Hebrews 10:30,31"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": "3",
          "title": "The Second Part : Of Man’s Deliverance",
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "q12",
              "label": "Q12",
              "question": "According to God’s righteous judgment we deserve punishment both in this world and forever after: how then can we escape this punishment and return to God’s favour?",
              "answer": "God requires that His justice be satisfied. Therefore the claims of His justice must be paid in full, either by ourselves, or by another.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Exodus.23_7",
                      "display": "Exodus 23:7"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Isaiah.53_11",
                      "display": "Isaiah 53:11"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.2_1-11",
                      "display": "Romans 2:1-11"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.8_3~4",
                      "display": "Romans 8:3,4"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q13",
              "label": "Q13",
              "question": "Can we pay this debt ourselves?",
              "answer": "Certainly not. Actually, we increase our guilt every day.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Matthew.6_12",
                      "display": "Matthew 6:12"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.2_4~5",
                      "display": "Romans 2:4,5"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q14",
              "label": "Q14",
              "question": "Can another creature - any at all - pay this debt for us?",
              "answer": "No. To begin with, God will not punish another creature for man’s guilt. Besides, no mere creature can bear the weight of God’s eternal anger against sin and release others from it.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Psalm.49_7-9",
                      "display": "Psalm 49:7-9"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Psalm.130_3",
                      "display": "Psalm 130:3"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Ezekiel.18_4~20",
                      "display": "Ezekiel 18:4,20"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Hebrews.2_14-18",
                      "display": "Hebrews 2:14-18"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q15",
              "label": "Q15",
              "question": "What kind of mediator and deliverer should we look for then?",
              "answer": "He must be truly human and truly righteous, yet more powerful than all creatures, that is, He must also be true God.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Isaiah.7_14",
                      "display": "Isaiah 7:14"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Isaiah.9_6",
                      "display": "Isaiah 9:6"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Isaiah.53_9",
                      "display": "Isaiah 53:9"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Jeremiah.23_6",
                      "display": "Jeremiah 23:6"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 5,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "John.1_1",
                      "display": "John 1:1"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 6,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.1_3",
                      "display": "Romans 1:3"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 7,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Corinthians.15_21",
                      "display": "1 Corinthians 15:21"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 8,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "2.Corinthians.5_21",
                      "display": "2 Corinthians 5:21"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 9,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Hebrews.2_17",
                      "display": "Hebrews 2:17"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 10,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Hebrews.7_26",
                      "display": "Hebrews 7:26"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q16",
              "label": "Q16",
              "question": "Why must He be truly human and truly righteous?",
              "answer": "God’s justice demands it: man has sinned, man must pay for his sin, but a sinner cannot pay for others.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.5_12~15",
                      "display": "Romans 5:12,15"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Corinthians.15_21",
                      "display": "1 Corinthians 15:21"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Hebrews.2_14-16",
                      "display": "Hebrews 2:14-16"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Hebrews.7_26~27",
                      "display": "Hebrews 7:26,27"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 5,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Peter.3_18",
                      "display": "1 Peter 3:18"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q17",
              "label": "Q17",
              "question": "Why must He also be true God?",
              "answer": "So that, by the power of His divinity, He might bear the weight of God’s anger in his humanity and earn for us and restore to us righteousness and life.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Isaiah.53",
                      "display": "Isaiah 53"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "John.3_16",
                      "display": "John 3:16"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "2.Corinthians.5_21",
                      "display": "2 Corinthians 5:21"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q18",
              "label": "Q18",
              "question": "And who is this mediator - true God and at the same time truly human and truly righteous?",
              "answer": "Our Lord Jesus Christ, who was given us to set us completely free and to make us right with God.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Matthew.1_21-23",
                      "display": "Matthew 1:21-23"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Luke.2_11",
                      "display": "Luke 2:11"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Corinthians.1_30",
                      "display": "1 Corinthians 1:30"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Timothy.2_5",
                      "display": "1 Timothy 2:5"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "q19",
              "label": "Q19",
              "question": "How do you come to know this?",
              "answer": "The holy gospel tells me. God Himself began to reveal the gospel already in Paradise; later, He proclaimed it by the holy patriarchs and prophets, and portrayed it by the sacrifices and other ceremonies of the law; finally, He fulfilled it through His own dear Son.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Genesis.3_15",
                      "display": "Genesis 3:15"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Genesis.22_18",
                      "display": "Genesis 22:18"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Genesis.49_10",
                      "display": "Genesis 49:10"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Leviticus.1-7",
                      "display": "Leviticus 1-7"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 5,
                  "refs": [
                    {
