              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c11_2",
              "label": "2",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "Faith, thus receiving and resting on Christ and His righteousness, is the alone instrument of justification: yet is it not alone in the person justified, but is ever accompanied with all other saving graces, and is no dead faith, but worketh by love.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "John.1_12",
                      "display": "John 1:12"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.3_28",
                      "display": "Romans 3:28"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.5_1",
                      "display": "Romans 5:1"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Galatians.5_6",
                      "display": "Galatians 5:6"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 5,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "James.2_17~22~26",
                      "display": "James 2:17,22,26"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c11_3",
              "label": "3",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "Christ, by His obedience and death, did fully discharge the debt of all those that are thus justified, and did make a proper, real, and full satisfaction to His Father’s justice in their behalf. Yet, inasmuch as He was given by the Father for them, and His obedience and satisfaction accepted in their stead, and both, freely, not for anything in them, their justification is only of free grace; that both the exact justice and rich grace of God might be glorified in the justification of sinners.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Isaiah.53_4-6~10-12",
                      "display": "Isaiah 53:4-6,10-12"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
