        {
          "number": "13",
          "title": "Of Sanctification",
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "c13_1",
              "label": "1",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "They who are effectually called and regenerated, having a new heart, and a new spirit created in them, are farther sanctified, really and personally, through the virtue of Christ’s death and resurrection, by His Word and Spirit dwelling in them: the dominion of the whole body of sin is destroyed, and the several lusts thereof are more and more weakened and mortified; and they more and more quickened and strengthened in all saving graces, to the practice of true holiness, without which no man shall see the Lord.",
