        {
          "number": "22",
          "title": "Of Lawful Oaths and Vows",
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "c22_1",
              "label": "1",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "A lawful oath is a part of religious worship, wherein, upon just occasion, the person swearing solemnly calleth God to witness what he asserteth, or promiseth, and to judge him according to the truth or falsehood of what he sweareth.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Exodus.20_7",
                      "display": "Exodus 20:7"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Leviticus.19_12",
                      "display": "Leviticus 19:12"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Deuteronomy.10_20",
                      "display": "Deuteronomy 10:20"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "2.Chronicles.6_22~23",
                      "display": "2 Chronicles 6:22,23"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 5,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "2.Corinthians.1_23",
                      "display": "2 Corinthians 1:23"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c22_2",
              "label": "2",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "The name of God only is that by which men ought to swear, and therein it is to be used with all holy fear and reverence. Therefore, to swear vainly, or rashly, by that glorious and dreadful Name; or, to swear at all by any other thing, is sinful, and to be abhorred. Yet, as in matters of weight and moment, an oath is warranted by the Word of God, under the New Testament as well as under the Old; so a lawful oath, being imposed by lawful authority, in such matters, ought to be taken.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Exodus.20_7",
                      "display": "Exodus 20:7"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Deuteronomy.6_13",
                      "display": "Deuteronomy 6:13"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
