                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": "23",
          "title": "Of the Civil Magistrate",
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "c23_1",
              "label": "1",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "God, the supreme Lord and King of all the world, hath ordained civil magistrates, to be under Him over the people, for His own glory, and the public good: and, to this end, hath armed them with the power of the sword, for the defence and encouragement of them that are good, and for the punishment of evil doers.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.13_1-4",
                      "display": "Romans 13:1-4"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Peter.2_13~14",
                      "display": "1 Peter 2:13,14"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c23_2",
              "label": "2",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "It is lawful for Christians to accept and execute the office of a magistrate, when called thereunto: in the managing whereof, as they ought especially to maintain piety, justice, and peace, according to the wholesome laws of each commonwealth; so, for that end, they may lawfully, now under the New Testament, wage war, upon just and necessary occasions.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "2.Samuel.23_3",
                      "display": "2 Samuel 23:3"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Psalm.2_10-12",
                      "display": "Psalm 2:10-12"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Psalm.82_3~4",
                      "display": "Psalm 82:3,4"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
