        {
          "number": "24",
          "title": "Of Marriage and Divorce",
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "c24_1",
              "label": "1",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "Marriage is to be between one man and one woman: neither is it lawful for any man to have more than one wife, nor for any woman to have more than one husband, at the same time.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Genesis.2_24",
                      "display": "Genesis 2:24"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Proverbs.2_17",
                      "display": "Proverbs 2:17"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Matthew.19_5~6",
                      "display": "Matthew 19:5,6"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c24_2",
              "label": "2",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "Marriage was ordained for the mutual help of husband and wife, for the increase of mankind with legitimate issue, and of the Church with an holy seed; and for preventing of uncleanness.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Genesis.2_18",
                      "display": "Genesis 2:18"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Malachi.2_15",
                      "display": "Malachi 2:15"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Corinthians.7_2~9",
                      "display": "1 Corinthians 7:2,9"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c24_3",
              "label": "3",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "It is lawful for all sorts of people to marry, who are able with judgment to give their consent. Yet it is the duty of Christians to marry only in the Lord. And therefore such as profess the true reformed religion should not marry with infidels, papists, or other idolaters: neither should such as are godly be unequally yoked, by marrying with such as are notoriously wicked in their life, or maintain damnable heresies.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Genesis.24_57~58",
                      "display": "Genesis 24:57,58"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Genesis.34_14",
                      "display": "Genesis 34:14"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
