                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 7,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.15_8",
                      "display": "Romans 15:8"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 8,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Corinthians.10_16~21",
                      "display": "1 Corinthians 10:16,21"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 9,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Corinthians.11_23~25~26",
                      "display": "1 Corinthians 11:23,25,26"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 10,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Galatians.3_17",
                      "display": "Galatians 3:17"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c27_2",
              "label": "2",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "There is, in every sacrament, a spiritual relation, or sacramental union, between the sign and the thing signified; whence it comes to pass, that the names and effects of the one are attributed to the other.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Genesis.17_10",
                      "display": "Genesis 17:10"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Matthew.26_27~28",
                      "display": "Matthew 26:27,28"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Titus.3_5",
                      "display": "Titus 3:5"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c27_3",
              "label": "3",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "The grace which is exhibited in or by the sacraments rightly used, is not conferred by any power in them; neither doth the efficacy of a sacrament depend upon the piety or intention of him that doth administer it; but, upon the work of the Spirit, and the word of institution, which contains, together with a precept authorising the use thereof, a promise of benefit to worthy receivers.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Matthew.3_11",
                      "display": "Matthew 3:11"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Matthew.26_27~28",
                      "display": "Matthew 26:27,28"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Matthew.28_19~20",
                      "display": "Matthew 28:19,20"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.2_28~29",
                      "display": "Romans 2:28,29"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 5,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Corinthians.12_13",
                      "display": "1 Corinthians 12:13"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 6,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Peter.3_21",
                      "display": "1 Peter 3:21"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c27_4",
              "label": "4",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "There be only two sacraments ordained by Christ our Lord in the Gospel; that is to say, Baptism, and the Supper of the Lord; neither of which may be dispensed by any, but by a minister of the Word lawfully ordained.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Matthew.28_19",
                      "display": "Matthew 28:19"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Corinthians.4_1",
                      "display": "1 Corinthians 4:1"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Corinthians.11_20~23",
                      "display": "1 Corinthians 11:20,23"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Hebrews.5_4",
                      "display": "Hebrews 5:4"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c27_5",
              "label": "5",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "The sacraments of the Old Testament, in regard of the spiritual things thereby signified and exhibited, were, for substance, the same with those of the new.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Corinthians.10_1-4",
                      "display": "1 Corinthians 10:1-4"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": "28",
          "title": "Of Baptism",
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "c28_1",
              "label": "1",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "Baptism is a sacrament of the new testament, ordained by Jesus Christ, not only for the solemn admission of the party baptised into the visible Church; but also, to be unto him a sign and seal of the covenant of grace, of his ingrafting into Christ, of regeneration, of remission of sins, and of his giving up unto God, through Jesus Christ, to walk in newness of life. Which sacrament is, by Christ’s own appointment, to be continued in His Church until the end of the world.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Matthew.28_19~20",
                      "display": "Matthew 28:19,20"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Mark.1_4",
