                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "2.Corinthians.7_1",
                      "display": "2 Corinthians 7:1"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 5,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Galatians.5_24",
                      "display": "Galatians 5:24"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 6,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Ephesians.3_16-19",
                      "display": "Ephesians 3:16-19"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 7,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Colossians.1_11",
                      "display": "Colossians 1:11"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 8,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Thessalonians.5_21-23",
                      "display": "1 Thessalonians 5:21-23"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 9,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Hebrews.12_14",
                      "display": "Hebrews 12:14"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c13_2",
              "label": "2",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "This sanctification is throughout the whole man, yet imperfect in this life; there abideth still some remnants of corruption in every part, whence ariseth a continual and irreconcilable war; the flesh lusting against the Spirit, and the Spirit against the flesh.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.7_18~23",
                      "display": "Romans 7:18,23"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Galatians.5_17",
                      "display": "Galatians 5:17"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Thessalonians.5_23",
                      "display": "1 Thessalonians 5:23"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "1.Peter.2_11",
                      "display": "1 Peter 2:11"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c13_3",
              "label": "3",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "In which war, although the remaining corruption for a time may much prevail, yet through the continual supply of strength from the sanctifying Spirit of Christ, the regenerate part doth overcome; and so the saints grow in grace, perfecting holiness in the fear of God, pressing after an heavenly life, in evangelical obedience to all the commands which Christ as Head and King, in His Word hath prescribed them.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.6_14",
                      "display": "Romans 6:14"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Romans.7_23",
                      "display": "Romans 7:23"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 3,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "2.Corinthians.3_18",
                      "display": "2 Corinthians 3:18"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "2.Corinthians.7_1",
                      "display": "2 Corinthians 7:1"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 5,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Ephesians.4_15~16",
                      "display": "Ephesians 4:15,16"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": "14",
          "title": "Of Saving Faith",
          "entries": [
            {
              "id": "c14_1",
              "label": "1",
              "question": null,
              "answer": "The grace of faith, whereby the elect are enabled to believe to the saving of their souls, is the work of the Spirit of Christ in their hearts, and is ordinarily wrought by the ministry of the Word; by which also, and by the administration of baptism and the Lord’s supper, prayer, and other means appointed of God, it is increased and strengthened.",
              "proofs": [
                {
                  "id": 1,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Luke.17_5",
                      "display": "Luke 17:5"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": 2,
                  "refs": [
                    {
                      "osis": "Acts.20_32",
